      "message": "I understand. Some tips; apologies if you know these already.\n\nTake care to give each CL a unique Change-Id. If you want to re-assign a Change-Id you can edit the description, delete the Change-Id and re-run git hooks. I keep my changes in different branches unless I\u0027m deliberately creating a relation chain.\n\nI also tend to keep the main branch without any of my local CLs; to sync with work in progress outstanding, I switch to the main branch, sync, then make new branches and re-patch the outstanding CLs. I find this much easier to handle merges than doing it in gclient sync.",
